---
import Page from "../layouts/page.astro";
import { supportEmail } from "../site";

const topics = [
  { id: "start", label: "Getting started" },
  { id: "pair", label: "Pairing with your partner" },
  { id: "widgets", label: "Adding widgets" },
  { id: "drawings", label: "Drawings on the Lock Screen" },
  { id: "notifications", label: "Notifications" },
  { id: "share", label: "Sharing to your wishlist" },
  { id: "new-phone", label: "Moving to a new iPhone" },
  { id: "unpair", label: "Unpair, block or report" },
  { id: "delete", label: "Deleting your account" },
];
const updated = "November 9, 2026";
---

<Page
  title="Ourio help: setup, pairing, widgets, notifications and your account"
  description="How to use Ourio on iPhone: set it up, pair with your partner, add the Lock Screen and Home Screen widgets, turn on notifications, share links to your wishlist, move to a new phone, unpair and delete your account."
>
  <section class="container-page pt-10 pb-24 md:pt-14">
    <p class="eyebrow">Help</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-[16ch] text-h2">Ourio help</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[42rem] text-lead text-soft">
      Short how-tos for Ourio, the iPhone app for couples. Ourio needs two iPhones on iOS 18 or later, one for each of you.
      Setup takes about two minutes.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-small text-muted">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-09">{updated}</time></p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,3fr)_minmax(0,9fr)] lg:gap-16">
      <nav aria-label="On this page" class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
        <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-small text-muted">
          {topics.map((topic) => <li><a href={`#${topic.id}`} class="hover:text-paper">{topic.label}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="doc [&>h2:first-child]:mt-0">
        <h2 id="start">Getting started</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Install Ourio from the App Store. There's no sign-up form: the app creates an anonymous account for you.</li>
          <li>Answer a few short questions, or skip any of them. If you're under 13, Ourio stops here.</li>
          <li>Tell Ourio when your story started (the Us tab counts your days together from it).</li>
          <li>Choose your cat's coat and name. Skip the name and she stays Mochi.</li>
          <li>Invite your partner (next section), turn on notifications and add a widget.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The app has four tabs: <strong>World</strong> (the room and Mochi), <strong>Moments</strong>, <strong>Shop</strong> and <strong>Us</strong>. The <strong>+</strong> button adds a Moment, a drawing, a note, a list item, a wish, an event or a date.</p>

        <h2 id="pair">Pairing with your partner</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>On the invite screen, Ourio shows your 10-character code.</li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Share invite</strong> to send it as a message or link, or show the QR code for your partner to scan.</li>
          <li>Your partner installs Ourio, taps <strong>I have an invite code</strong> and pastes or types it.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          A code works for 24 hours; after that, open the invite screen again for a new one. A room holds exactly two people. More in <a href="/how-it-works/">how pairing works</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="widgets">Adding widgets</h2>
        <h3>Home Screen</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Touch and hold an empty spot on the Home Screen until the apps jiggle, then tap <strong>Edit</strong> › <strong>Add Widget</strong>.</li>
          <li>Search for <strong>Ourio</strong>, choose a widget (Our Corner, Ourio, Block or Drawing) and a size, and tap <strong>Add Widget</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>Lock Screen</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Touch and hold the Lock Screen, tap <strong>Customize</strong>, then <strong>Lock Screen</strong>.</li>
          <li>Tap the widget area under the clock and add <strong>Us</strong>, <strong>Note</strong> or <strong>Drawing</strong> from Ourio.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Some widgets have buttons: set your mood or tick a list item without opening the app. In Control Center you can add
          <strong>Pet Your Cat</strong> and <strong>New Note</strong>. See <a href="/features/widgets-and-notifications/">every widget and size</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="drawings">Drawings on the Lock Screen</h2>
        <p>
          Tap <strong>+</strong> › <strong>Draw</strong>. The canvas shows your partner's Lock Screen so you see where the
          drawing will sit. When you send it, your partner gets a notification and the <strong>Drawing</strong> widget shows it.
          Without the widget, they open it from the notification. iOS doesn't let apps change the wallpaper, so the
          widget is how drawings reach the Lock Screen.
        </p>

        <h2 id="notifications">Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          Ourio only notifies you about your partner: a new drawing, photo or note, a heart on your photo, a Pick tonight match,
          their turn in a game, and reminders before a date you planned. If they stopped arriving, open iPhone
          <strong>Settings</strong> › <strong>Notifications</strong> › <strong>Ourio</strong> and turn on
          <strong>Allow Notifications</strong>. Focus modes can hold them back too.
        </p>

        <h2 id="share">Sharing to your wishlist</h2>
        <p>
          In Safari or another app, tap <strong>Share</strong> and choose <strong>Ourio</strong>. If you don't see it, scroll
          the row of apps and tap <strong>More</strong>. <strong>Add to my wishlist</strong> opens with the link filled in;
          add a price or details and tap <strong>Add wish</strong>. Links and text can be shared, not images.
        </p>

        <h2 id="new-phone">Moving to a new iPhone</h2>
        <p>
          Your account key lives in your iCloud Keychain, so on a new iPhone signed in to the same Apple Account, opening Ourio
          brings your account back. If you linked <strong>Save your cat and notes</strong> (Sign in with Apple), you can also
          sign in that way.
        </p>

        <h2 id="unpair">Unpair, block or report</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Settings</strong> in Ourio and find the <strong>Partner</strong> section.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Unpair</strong>: you stop sharing with each other. The shared room, notes, photos, cat and activity are deleted for both of you; each keeps what they bought and half the coins. You can pair again with a new code.</li>
          <li><strong>Block partner</strong>: you are unpaired, and neither of you can pair with the other again.</li>
          <li><strong>Report partner</strong>: tell us about harassment, inappropriate content, spam or not feeling safe. We read every report.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="delete">Deleting your account</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Settings</strong> › <strong>Delete account</strong>. Your account and what you sent are deleted from the
          server, your partner is unpaired, and everything on this phone is erased. This can't be undone. Deleting the app alone
          doesn't remove your data from our server. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Still stuck?</h2>
        <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> or see <a href="/support/">Support</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
